    type: "section"
    title: "A Beat Late"
    excerpt: "By the second morning the egg was warmer than the feed-sack sling, the sling was warmer than Boof's ribs, and the maps in the town archive were still pretending none of this was a fact. She had walked downhill the way..."
    route: ^[chapter/02/s01]{open}
  }
  s02: <
    handle: "custom-boof/02"
    type: "custom-boof"
    excerpt: "The incomplete maps had led her here—the grove beyond the last honest furrow, a place the town labeled as reserve growth and the workers called the listening thicket. Every step pressed a different forgotten fragment ..."
    route: ^[chapter/02/s02]{open}
  >
  s03: <
    handle: "custom-boonberry/03"
    type: "custom-boonberry"
    excerpt: "The berries here did not shine for harvest distribution. They shone like grains under stress—bright when a phrase repeated often enough to become policy, dim when the thicket put them back to sleep. Boof recognized se..."
